  "note": "Where an animal lives, at the resolution a child needs: a part of the world, not a country and not a habitat map. Points are representative places inside the district, used to stand markers on the globe. spreadDegrees is how far animals scatter around a district point, so a savanna full of animals does not stack them all on one spot. isGeneric marks districts that span the world — oceans, rivers, \"everywhere\" — which are never used to fill a country with animals it does not have. isMarine marks water districts; an animal that only lives in water is never stood inside a country.",
